<!--
    Darwin AArch64 stack probe (`option chkstkdarwin on|off`, default on).

    Apple clang calls ___chkstk_darwin, with the byte count in x9, before it
    allocates a frame larger than a page or a variable-length array. The probe
    writes no register but x9, x16/x17 and the flags, and the code after it
    reads the argument registers. The AArch64 prototype model kills x0, x1 and
    x8-x18 at every call, so those reads became the probe's return value or a
    register nothing assigns, and the functions lost their parameters.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 flow classification. The action in
    p2_lift/kuna_chkstkdarwin.rs removes the probe call from the raw p-code
    before FuncLink and SSA.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes clear it
    and load chkstkdarwin_macho_arm64 (source chkstkdarwin.c, recipe in
    chkstkdarwin_macho_arm64.provenance) through the object bootstrap:
      _big_frame   20,000-byte frame, probe called through the GOT
                   (adrp x16; ldr x16,[x16]; blr x16), k read from w0 after it
      _vla_last    variable-length array, probe called through the GOT, the
                   index read from w0 and the size from x1 after it
      _probe_stub  the probe called with bl through its __stubs entry, x0 and x1
                   read after it
      0x100000520  that __stubs entry itself: its br x16 to the probe is a jump,
                   with no code after it, so it is left alone in both passes

      chkstkdarwin_macho_arm64e (arm64e; source chkstkdarwin_arm64e.s, recipe
      in the fixtures README): _big_e reaches the probe through its __auth_ptr
      slot with adrp/ldr/blraaz x16, _vla_e with adrp x17/add/ldr x16,[x17]/
      blraa x16,x17; authptrcall names the slot, so the same walk matches
      chkstkdarwin_elf_aarch64 (AArch64 ELF; chkstkdarwin_elf_aarch64.s):
      caller calls a defined function that is only named ___chkstk_darwin
      and returns its result + 1; outside an Apple image the call stays

    Pass 1 (`option chkstkdarwin off`) reproduces the bug: each function takes
    no parameter and assigns the probe's "result".
    Pass 2 is the shipped default: the probe calls are gone and every function
    takes its parameters again.

    Assertions span the combined output of both passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
